{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790447295,"nonce":"JfV0JmcLnCDYgVyEE6IT/jdyRTs=","title":"super.m() inside an override of a @:native method is typed Dynamic","message":"`class Base { @:native(\"renamed\") public function original():String return \"B\"; }` / `class Derived extends Base { override public function original():String return super.original() + \"D\"; }`: `d.original()` prints `\u003cunknown type N\u003eD`. try_super_call lowers the call, but its result is cast string -\u003e *void and concatenated through the Dynamic-to-string path, so the super call's type is Dynamic in TAST (super method lookup misses the @:native-renamed parent method's type). Found while writing the ReflectDynamicCalls fixture.","files":null}]}